  "description": "KUPHUZ crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H78 Gd6 N12 O36,8(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.775-3.775 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.51-111.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C44H110Gd6N12O44. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 Htea (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
